Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: The Red Pennant Bites the Salt
- Story & Context: When a rogue freak wave swamped the harbor workshop of Morne-Rouge during the 1998 solstice tide, the band salvage-wired their meteorite-rigged fuzz pedals directly to the local lighthouse generator to record the opening track before the power died. Bassist Jules ran his vintage valve amp through a rusted brass ship-horn, capturing a raw, clipped low-end that shook loose white coral dust from the sea wall while singer Mara screamed over the swell. The resulting session captured an accidental, explosive collision of garage-punk fury and blinding synth-brass light that defined the genre's birthed sound. "Rip down the signal rag and let the breaker take us!" Mara howled into a ocean-drenched ribbon mic as the tides rose over their boots.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: High-contrast vintage photograph of a storm-battered lighthouse gleaming on a rocky ocean point under a brilliant red signal flag, with giant emerald-green waves exploding into white foam against copper synth gear setup on the wet rocks, drenched in warm tropical sunlight.

Track 2: Carbet Code (Souse the Lantern)
- Story & Context: Written as a quiet confession by synthesist Chantal after losing her uncle’s vintage brass pocket-chronometer to the harbor mud, this track slows the tempo to a hypnotic, sun-dazed coasting speed. She mapped the micro-timing glitches of the chronometer’s missing escape wheel directly onto a patch of soaring synth brass that warbles like heat waves off black asphalt. Recorded late at night in a empty sardine cannery using a single microphone hanging from the rafters, the track captures the sound of rain tapping on tin while fuzz-guitar notes decay endlessly into the wet air. "Souse the lantern, child, the tide knows where we sleep," she sings softly in a raspy, sun-dried whisper over drone chords that wobble with mechanical fragility.
