Track 3: Old-Man-Lanyard’s Brass Astrolabe
- Story & Context: The final track on the EP grew into a local urban legend after the band performed it continuously for six hours straight during the annual Saint-Pierre harbor festival, refusing to stop even when the rain turned to heavy volcanic haze. Built around a single motorik garage drum beat and a rising three-note synth-brass fanfare, the track incorporates actual audio recordings of old meteorite fragments being struck with bronze tuning forks. By the time the final feedback loop faded, the local fishermen swore the brass gears inside the lighthouse clock had synchronized themselves to the song’s 120 BPM pulse. "He mapped the fallen star right off the harbor chart!" shouts the chorus as a wall of glowing, ocean-soaked distortion swallows the brass hooks whole.
